{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 biographical drama film written by aaron sorkin and directed by david fincher. the film is based on the true story of the founding of mark zuckerberg and his creation of the social networking site facebook.\n\nthe film starts with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, a brilliant and awkward high school student who creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. this site quickly becomes popular, but also attracts the attention of the university's administration, which threatens to shut it down.\n\nmark meets dylan, played by armie hammer, and the two become friends and business partners. they come up with the idea for a new website that will allow users to connect with each other and share information. they call it \"thefacebook,\" and it quickly gains popularity.\n\nas thefacebook grows in popularity, mark and dylan face growing competition from other websites, including a rival site called \"connecticut\" that is owned by the winklevoss twins, cambridge and tyler, played by armie hammer and roger l. rees. the twins accuse mark and dylan of copying their idea and sue them for intellectual property infringement.\n\nmeanwhile, mark's relationship with his friends and classmates, including eduardo, played by andrew garfield, and divya, played by rinko kikuchi, is put to the test as he becomes increasingly obsessed with facebook. his relationship with his girlfriend, emily, played by kirsten dunst, begins to suffer as well.\n\nthe film also explores the theme of the impact that facebook has on society. as the site grows in popularity, people become increasingly dependent on it and begin to lose touch with reality. the film shows how facebook can be used for both positive and negative purposes.\n\nthe film features strong performances from the cast, particularly jesse eisenberg, who brings a sense of vulnerability and intensity to his portrayal of mark zuckerberg. armie hammer also gives a strong performance as dylan, and the chemistry between the two actors is palpable.\n\nthe film's script is witty and engaging, and the direction by david finch is excellent. the film's use of music and cinematography is also noteworthy. the film's score, which was composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is haunting and memorable.\n\noverall, the social network is a film that is both entertaining and thought-provoking. it is a cautionary tale about the dangers of unchecked ambition and the impact that technology can have on society. it is also a testament to the power of creativity and innovation.\n\nrating: 5/5 stars", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.20552276074886322}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00035589560866355896}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04680097848176956}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0009609610424377024}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.5923129320144653}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -2.7847750186920166}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -9.179073458653875e-06}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.002908050548285246}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0016281455755233765}, {"token": " written", "logprob": -2.489727258682251}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.39662453532218933}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.2868504524230957}, {"token": "aron", "logprob": -0.0003228858404327184}, {"token": " s", "logprob": -0.0014968630857765675}, {"token": "ork", "logprob": -6.55629628454335e-05}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.18293195962905884}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -4.184158387943171e-05}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.096749536